<h3 id=3D"online-presence">Online presence</h3>
<p>An online presence indicator is an essential feature of many chat applic=
ations. Usually, you can see a green dot next to a user=E2=80=99s profile p=
icture or username. This section explains what happens behind the scenes.</=
p>
<p>In the high-level design, presence servers are responsible for managing =
online status and communicating with clients through WebSocket. There are a=
 few flows that will trigger online status change. Let us examine each of t=
hem.</p>
<h4 id=3D"user-login">User login</h4>
<p>The user login flow is explained in the =E2=80=9CService Discovery=E2=80=
=9D section. After a WebSocket connection is built between the client and t=
he real-time service, user A=E2=80=99s online status and <em>last_active_at=
</em> timestamp are saved in the KV store. Presence indicator shows the use=
r is online after she logs in.</p>
